  "body": "This conditional precision audit completes the explicit PR1054 substitution left open in PR1278. With the common immutable operator and inherited preparation/leaf contracts, PR1085's sharp prefix count and PR1278's squarefree commuting intervals replace the generic interval factor `C\u00b2G\u00b2` by `C\u00b2G`. The negative leaf is bounded at its positive preimage; the complete beta^-8 internal reserve remains paid.\n\nFor PR1054's radix-64 example (`p=128,m=20,w_input=0`), sufficient fractional width falls **1,420,902 \u2192 1,162,598**, saving **258,304 bits**; signed integer width falls **1,291,719 \u2192 1,291,709**. Factor preparation remains 516,499 bits, with the same 4,000 leaves and six borrowed arrays. The proved convenient fractional envelope is `max(p,w_input)+m+15r\u00b3`, versus PR1054's `18r\u00b3`; no optimal-width, measured-speedup, supplier or kappa claim.\n\nOnly `research/commuting-dirty-precision/` is added. It contains the complete written substitution and cost bill, exact formulas, source pins, frozen consumed source subset, deterministic evidence, controls and registered replay. No selected record or upstream source is changed.\n\n### Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/commuting-dirty-precision\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_COMMUTING_DIRTY_PRECISION`, six passing package groups and `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE`.\n\n- 5,220 exact prime-power budget certificates through radix 512 and 216 generic rational cases.\n- 78 literal PR1054/PR628 dispatcher comparisons, 150,126 leaf events, both signs and shared scratch.\n- 20 actual stable rational fixtures: **80 signed rounded words / 2,336 leaves**, all with nonzero errors. Exact dirty restoration, standalone negative calls, finite-geometric ideal oracle, inverse-preimage guards, literal read/write and full routing counts pass. Each forward census matches the old finer-grid execution on identical incoming data.\n- Eight mathematical/admission controls; five actual package corruptions reject and read-only relocated inputs pass. Registered replay on CPython 3.12.13: **60.128 s**. All 25 selected-record tests and the selected-record integrity check pass. The clean patch applies to refreshed main.\n\nThe million-bit radix-64 row is an exact budget computation, not a literal execution. Full PR1054 tests, selected supplier cold replay, full factor preparation, hosted CI, native/physical integration and proof-assistant verification were not run. The all-size claim rests on the written proof and pinned predecessor lemmas, not finite extrapolation. PR1085's similar 1,162,523 figure concerns PR905's different leaf budget.\n\n### Pins, overlap and credit\n\nResearch base `dadfea6e8a78ff6ba901705f87532a71c6f5bbb8`; refreshed main `bdd4c63ac7c5d8a46ce070ba133df8d7ba9cb92c` leaves selected/guidance inputs unchanged. Seed **64**, adversarial audit. Claim: discussion #1283. Fresh overlap read covered 815 open PR bodies and 21 discussion records; exact dependency heads remain unchanged. No matching rounded-contract substitution found; this is bounded overlap evidence, not a novelty guarantee.\n\nCredit **Ali Romman** (#1054 at `6bc675be1554b3a3be771147f21f9dc2c6dae50a`), **Hanson Sun** (#1085 at `82b99c7d12dac009d35636562df4c6c91e885409`, #1244), **Charles Bethin** (#1278 at `06b8c006891ae78abe24b30d2fe9d8c188deafe8`), Chafik Boukhalfa's #628/#862/#905, Gareth Davidson's #877, 0xkilgore's #663 and the retained lineage. These pending dependencies are explicitly pinned; their GitHub state is not mathematical acceptance.\n\nPrepared for **Philipp (@mightyOil)** with substantial **OpenAI Codex / GPT-6 Astra assistance** in mathematics, code, verification and writing. Apache-2.0; no independent human-review or literature-priority claim. The README gives concrete open next questions on sharp interval coefficients and complete caller admission.\n\nConcurrent #1294 (`03025ca1d51091a9525203000e77dacccfa6a70d`) supplies universal local phase-algebra certificates for #1278; this is complementary, with no imported implementation. The cost proof explicitly distinguishes data length `M_len` from interval norm bound `L`.\n",
